Diagnostic-only patch for torch_spyre/_inductor/dedup_constants.py at a9316b3.

Adds sub-timers and a gold-vs-name_to_users comparison, gated on
TORCH_SPYRE_DEDUP_DIAG=1. When the env var is unset the code paths
are inert; the pass runs unchanged (identical Python semantics as
today's implementation).

Apply on the pod as:

    cd $HOME/pr3806/torch-spyre
    git checkout a9316b381 --detach                            # or a fresh worktree
    git apply --3way path/to/dedup_diagnostics.patch
    # Also place dedup_diagnostics.py next to the target file:
    cp path/to/dedup_diagnostics.py \
        torch_spyre/_inductor/dedup_diagnostics.py

Verify: with TORCH_SPYRE_DEDUP_DIAG unset, the pass' Python behavior
is unchanged. With TORCH_SPYRE_DEDUP_DIAG=1 and SPYRE_DEDUP_DIAG_OUT
pointing to a writable JSON path, an atexit hook writes the records.
Set SPYRE_DEDUP_DIAG_MAX_PER_DUPLICATE to cap per-duplicate records
if a very-large workload would blow up the JSON (default 10000).

The diff below was generated with ``diff -u`` against a9316b3's
pristine ``torch_spyre/_inductor/dedup_constants.py``. To regenerate:

    diff -u --label a/torch_spyre/_inductor/dedup_constants.py \
             --label b/torch_spyre/_inductor/dedup_constants.py \
             ORIGINAL DIAGNOSED > dedup_diagnostics.patch

